WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:06.880
Hi, Mystery Recapped here. Today I am&nbsp;
going to explain a short Drama film called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:16.400
“The Karman Line.” Spoilers&nbsp;
ahead! Watch out and take care!
&nbsp;

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:21.600
The protagonist of the movie is a middle-aged&nbsp;
housewife named Sarah. She lives with her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:28.080
teenage daughter Carly and her husband Dave.&nbsp;
One afternoon Sarah is in a delightful mood.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:32.720
She is blasting a romantic song on the&nbsp;
radio and is dancing around the house.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:38.800
At the same time, Carly returns home from school&nbsp;
and is in a seemingly bad mood. She takes off her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:44.400
dirty shoes and carelessly tosses them away. Her&nbsp;
mother tries to lighten her mood by dancing and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:50.080
singing around her but she doesn’t acknowledge&nbsp;
it, and rather finds it annoying. Sarah follows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:55.680
her to the kitchen while still dancing but Carly&nbsp;
simply turns the radio’s volume down and takes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:00.720
the dinner plate from the counter. It is evident&nbsp;
that Carly doesn’t appreciate her mother's efforts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:06.080
and takes her for granted. Sarah, however, doesn't&nbsp;
seem to mind her daughter’s indifference. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:11.760
simply turns the volume back up and checks Carly’s&nbsp;
bag to see if she has eaten all her food. 
&nbsp;

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:16.720
Sarah then finds a test paper inside her&nbsp;
bag that has very bad grades. Although it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:22.560
is only a mock test she urges her daughter to&nbsp;
do better. Carly, again ignores her which has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:28.160
become sort of a routine in the household. When&nbsp;
Sarah asks for an answer, she simply walks away&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:33.840
to her room. Moments later, Sarah picks up her&nbsp;
drink from the living room’s coffee table but it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:40.320
drops from her hand. She starts to panic and yells&nbsp;
for help as her feet begin to move on their own.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:46.400
Carly hears her cry and quickly runs downstairs&nbsp;
to see her mother is levitating off the ground.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:51.920
She is too stunned to speak. In the following&nbsp;
scene, three men are trying to bring Sarah back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:57.440
to the ground. One of them is her husband Dave.&nbsp;
He holds her hand for emotional support as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:03.120
other two guys pull Sarah down. They try their&nbsp;
best but do not succeed. It is almost as if they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:12.080
are working against a mysterious force that is&nbsp;
keeping her afloat. No matter how much they try,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:16.240
she doesn’t budge from her place. 
Carly watches them from the door, not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:22.160
being able to comprehend what is going on. The men&nbsp;
leave a while later but Sarah keeps levitating.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:28.160
Dave then calls their family doctor, Dr. Behringer&nbsp;
to inspect the situation. He measures the distance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:32.880
she has elevated from the ground and finds&nbsp;
out that she is going higher over time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:38.400
This worries the entire family. Even the doctor&nbsp;
does not have an answer as to how it is possible.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:43.520
He simply takes her blood sample to study it and&nbsp;
hopefully find out why gravity has stopped working&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:49.280
on her. He also promises to send in a consultant,&nbsp;
Dr. Benham who can potentially help her. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:54.160
husband asks him how long it will take but the&nbsp;
doctor assures them that since Sarah is healthy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:59.040
there are all the reasons to believe she will&nbsp;
be better in no time. Starting that day, Sarah&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:05.520
cannot move around and keeps on flying upwards. In&nbsp;
only one day, she stands taller than her husband.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:13.360
Dave buys a bedpan to help her defecate but their&nbsp;
hopes of her getting better are fading with time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:18.320
Since she cannot move from the room, the father&nbsp;
and daughter redecorate it to fit her needs and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:24.080
keep her entertained. Soon, Sarah’s sisters&nbsp;
also come to her house to help her with life.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:27.760
It is almost as if she is bedridden&nbsp;
and needs people to take care of her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:32.640
They clean up after her every day. Eventually,&nbsp;
they start needing a ladder to reach her.
&nbsp;

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:37.680
Dr. Behringer visits regularly to check up on&nbsp;
Sarah and measure how much she has elevated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:42.640
since the last time. He keeps track of the maths&nbsp;
and finds out that she is being pulled up at a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:48.560
higher rate as time passes by. To stop this, he&nbsp;
makes her wear a belt with weights inside of it so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:53.920
the weights would decrease the rate of elevation.&nbsp;
However, this doesn’t help Sarah’s case and she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:58.640
almost reaches the ceiling. Dave starts getting&nbsp;
frustrated seeing no results out of the doctor’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:04.240
experiments. At night, Sarah starts wrapping a&nbsp;
blanket around herself while sleeping on air.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:09.280
Dave loves his wife dearly and makes sure to&nbsp;
be with her all the time. He has shifted from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:14.000
the bedroom to the living room to be with her&nbsp;
at night in case she needs anything. Sarah’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:20.320
consultant Dr. Mary Benham only arrives after&nbsp;
a week. By the time, Sarah is on the ceiling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:25.440
struggling to go further up. The doctor introduces&nbsp;
herself and reaches out to shake her hand.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:30.560
She apologizes for not getting there sooner and&nbsp;
inquires how they are coping with the situation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:34.640
Dave jokes and says that the ceiling is&nbsp;
not a convenient place to keep a wife. 
&nbsp;

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:42.800
For some reason, the doctor doesn’t seem to be&nbsp;
surprised by Sarah’s condition. She simply brings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:47.680
out a measuring tape and measures the distance&nbsp;
between her and the floor. Dave offers the doctor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:53.440
a cup of tea and sends Carly to make it. Without&nbsp;
Sarah’s help, the kitchen is a complete mess.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:58.240
Carly brings out a dirty mug from the sink and&nbsp;
simply rinses it before pouring tea in it and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:06.720
handing it to the doctor. After realizing the&nbsp;
severeness of Sarah’s condition, the doctor’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:11.920
demeanor changes. The family had been waiting&nbsp;
for her to come and miraculously cure Sarah,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:17.520
but they soon realise that she, too, has no idea&nbsp;
what the problem is. The doctor bluntly tells&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:23.200
the family that their case is unique, so nothing&nbsp;
is certain. From what the doctors have seen and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:28.720
studied, Sarah will continue to move upwards at&nbsp;
a variable but increasing rate. Dave hesitantly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:33.920
asks the doctor if she can bring Sarah down to&nbsp;
which she apologizes and says she can’t. 
&nbsp;

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:38.720
The weights will slow her process but if she&nbsp;
carries more of it, it will injure her. Their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:44.560
best bet is to wait for the condition to go away&nbsp;
on its own. In about ten weeks, Sarah will reach a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:50.080
height of twelve thousand feet. From there, she&nbsp;
will need oxygen to survive. Even after that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:55.360
she will still keep rising upwards and they will&nbsp;
have to keep her warm and control her diet. Sarah&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.360 --> 00:06:00.960
finally comes to the conclusion that she cannot&nbsp;
be saved. The family also acknowledges she is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:06.160
going to rise to the sky until her inevitable&nbsp;
death. Carly comments that her mother is going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:12.240
into orbit. Dave loses patience and demands the&nbsp;
doctor to do something but she says she can only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:18.480
do the best to keep her comfortable but there is&nbsp;
no known way to save her. At night, Dave cuts the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:24.480
floor around Sarah’s head to let her fly up. He is&nbsp;
aggressive while cutting it and almost hurts her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:35.120
As the dust falls on the poor woman, she calls&nbsp;
for her daughter for help. However, Carly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:42.560
entirely ignores her mother’s pleas and turns&nbsp;
the tap on to not hear her. Eventually, Dave&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:48.160
completes making the hole and holds his wife's&nbsp;
hand. Sarah’s head is now inside Carly’s room.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:53.520
She is clearly bothered by her mother invading her&nbsp;
privacy although she has no control over it.
&nbsp;

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:59.200
The following day, Carly is studying for her&nbsp;
final exams as Sarah watches her in silence.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:04.560
She has to pee but doesn’t want to disturb her&nbsp;
daughter. Sometime later, she apologizes and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:10.720
asks Carly to call her father. Carly simply brings&nbsp;
the bedpan and helps her. Following that, she sits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:15.680
back to study but cannot focus with her mother&nbsp;
in the room. Carly tells her that she cannot take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:20.960
the exams this year because of the situation but&nbsp;
Sarah lashes out at her. She doesn’t want to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:27.040
a drawback in her daughter’s life. Some days later&nbsp;
is Dave and Sarah’s anniversary. They have invited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:31.920
Sarah’s sister to dress her up for the occasion.&nbsp;
Dave compliments her, saying that she looks like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:37.920
an angel, and the two laugh at the irony. Even&nbsp;
at the time of crisis, the couple celebrates and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:44.080
drinks together. Dave gets on a table and kisses&nbsp;
her. Eventually, the two have intercourse. When&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:49.840
Carly returns home from school one day, she hears&nbsp;
her mother moaning in pain. It turns out that Dave&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:55.280
has tied her leg to the ground to keep her from&nbsp;
flying away which is really painful for her. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.280 --> 00:08:00.720
sits on the door, not being able to watch his wife&nbsp;
whimper in misery. Carly quickly runs upstairs and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:05.760
gets a knife to cut the rope. In the following&nbsp;
scene, Sarah has reached outside the house. 
&nbsp;

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:10.800
Dave and Carly reach her using a crane to hand&nbsp;
her food and supplies. This is probably the last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:15.200
time they are going to see her, so they pack&nbsp;
her with enough food, oxygen, and water for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:20.320
her journey to the sky. Carly hands her a phone&nbsp;
and a battery to call home when needed. She has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:25.200
also brought a music player so Sarah can listen&nbsp;
to all her favorite songs when she gets bored.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:30.160
Following that, she is made to wear a heavy&nbsp;
backpack so she would elevate at a slower speed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:35.840
As the daughter hands her the rations, Dave stays&nbsp;
quiet and only watches them. Before leaving, he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:42.160
hugs his wife tightly, knowing that she is never&nbsp;
coming back. The family shares a tearful goodbye.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:47.840
The next day, we see Sarah way high up in the sky.&nbsp;
She is hardly visible from the ground. To pass&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:53.280
time, she is invested in a crossword puzzle.&nbsp;
Suddenly, a drop of water falls on her book.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:58.480
As she wipes it away it starts to drizzle. She&nbsp;
takes off her hat and wears the hood of her jacket&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:04.320
to keep warm. Some more days later, Sarah uses&nbsp;
binoculars to look down at the earth. She brings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:09.280
out a packet of biscuits that Carly had given&nbsp;
her and sees that she is almost out of them.
&nbsp;

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:13.600
She calls Carly and asks her what she is&nbsp;
cooking for herself. Without her mother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:20.880
she has started to eat baked beans and&nbsp;
toast every day. Sarah worries about her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:26.160
and tells her to eat well-cooked food, but&nbsp;
Carly is clearly not interested in talking.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:30.640
She answers in single words, mostly because&nbsp;
it is overwhelming to talk to her mother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:35.760
knowing that she will die one of these days. Sarah&nbsp;
apologizes for disturbing her and claims that she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:41.200
misses her but Carly hangs up the call before she&nbsp;
can finish. Sarah gets emotional after the call,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:46.160
so she brings out her music player to help her&nbsp;
calm down. But to her misfortune, she accidentally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:52.320
drops it. For some seconds, she loses her calm&nbsp;
and screams in frustration. Her screams invite a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:57.600
flock of birds towards her which instantly cheers&nbsp;
her mood. She waves her hands around happily in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:03.360
between them. Dave misses his wife dearly and&nbsp;
resorts to alcoholism to get rid of the pain.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:08.000
One night, it starts to rain heavily. Although&nbsp;
Sarah is wearing thick clothes, they are not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:13.360
enough to keep her warm. She misses her family&nbsp;
but can do nothing about it. She somehow survives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:18.400
the night, holding herself to keep warm.
The following day, she reaches higher in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:24.320
sky and now requires an oxygen mask to survive.&nbsp;
She removes the mask and calls her husband.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.880 --> 00:10:30.000
Dave runs to the phone and asks her if she is&nbsp;
doing well. Carly also comes running worried&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:35.680
about her mother. Sarah tells Carly that even&nbsp;
if she fails her exams, she is very proud of her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:40.480
and will always love her. Dave repeatedly&nbsp;
asks her to put the oxygen mask back on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:46.880
but she refuses. Instead, she asks them to stand&nbsp;
away from the hole in the ceiling. Seconds later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:52.400
a bag falls through it. The two register that&nbsp;
Sarah has decided to stop holding onto her life.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:58.400
Carly falls to the floor and hugs the bag begging&nbsp;
for her mother to return. As the sun rises,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:04.720
Sarah flies faster into the sky. With a smile on&nbsp;
her face, she tells her husband that she loves him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:09.920
and puts the phone down. A while later, the&nbsp;
phone falls through the ceiling. The father&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:15.840
and the daughter hold each other and cry mourning&nbsp;
Sarah’s death. It is now a few weeks after the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:21.520
incident. The family has repaired the ceiling.&nbsp;
Carly prepares tea and breakfast for both of them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.520 --> 00:11:27.360
and studies hard for her finals. Dave notices&nbsp;
a change in her behavior after Sarah’s death.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.360 --> 00:11:33.120
The movie ends as they eat the meal in silence.
